8.35 evā cana, bhajā rāye, rarimā te, bhajā bhūri, / śrudhī naḥ, ubhayatrā te, bhajā tvam, and mṛḷayā naḥ ca.

8.36 In an eleven-syllable and twelve-syllable verse-quarter (pāda), the eighth syllable, when light (laghu), [is lengthened] at the time of the continuous text (saṃhitā), when a [light syllable] follows;

8.39 And the sixth syllable in an eight-syllable [verse-quarter (pāda)];

8.40 The full count should be observed through resolutions (vyūha) when deficient in syllables possessing an uncombined semivowel resulting from kṣaipra sandhi;

8.41 But not in vāvṛdhanta, vātasya, avadyāni, jighāṃsasi, / sāsahyāma, vavṛtyāma, dīdihi, nor the eighth in ūrṇuhi,

